# GitHub releases

When the user asks to commit, push, ship, or cut a build/release:

1. Bump version in `src/WinterMP.Core/WinterMP.Core.csproj`, `src/WinterMP.Launcher/WinterMP.Launcher.csproj`, `src/WinterMP.Launcher/Assets/wintermp-compat.json` (`modVersion` + `protocolVersion`), and `installer/WinterMP.iss` when the change is user-facing.
2. Build release artifacts:
   - **Routine updates:** `.\tools\quick-ship.ps1 -Notes "..."` (or `ship-release.ps1 -Fast -SkipFetch`) — payload + launcher zips only (~30–40s).
   - **New installs / full release:** `.\tools\ship-release.ps1 -NonInteractive -Notes "..."` — also builds `OurWinterCar-Setup.exe` via Inno (~60–90s).
3. Commit and push source changes.
4. Create or update the GitHub release with `gh release create` (or `gh release edit` if retagging the same version):
   - Tag `v{version}` on the pushed commit
   - Title `v{version} - Our Winter Car`
   - Release notes: download link, what's new, quick start (match prior releases)
   - Assets: at minimum `dist/OurWinterCar-payload.zip` + `dist/OurWinterCar-Launcher-win-x64.zip`; add `dist/OurWinterCar-Setup.exe` on full ships
5. Do not skip the release step when pushing build-worthy changes — code on `main` without a matching release leaves players on stale binaries.
